If you go directly from the black point to the blue point, you see $x_a$ went down by about $1.2$ units. But two things could have happened:
$\bullet$ Starting point: $w = 10$, $U = 10$, $x_a = 5$, $x_b = 5$ (prices $p = (1,1)$).
$\bullet$ After price change to $p' = (1,2)$:
\quad \emph{Case B (income effect only):} $w = 10$, $x_a = 5$, $x_b = 2.5$.
